# Custom server support for TanStack Start #3777
created: 2025-03-14, last updated: 2025-10-14, [Read more](https://github.com/TanStack/router/discussions/3777)

When it was still Vinxi-based, it was possible to set up a router for a WebSocket handler by modifying the `vinxiApp` instance directly:
> `app.config.ts`
```
import { defineConfig } from '@tanstack/react-start/config'
defineConfig({
// TanStack Start config
}).then(vinxiApp => {
return vinxiApp.addRouter({
name: 'websocket',
type: 'http',
target: 'server',
base: '/api/ws',
handler: 'app/routes/api/ws.ts'
})
})
```

